9}, where H_n is the nth harmonic number. Because H_{2020} = sum_{k=1}^{2020} 1/k, and H_{1999} = sum_{k=1}^{1999} 1/k, so their difference is sum_{k=2000}^{2020} 1/k.\n\nSimilarly, sum_{n=2000}^{2020} 1 = 21 terms, so 21.\n\nTherefore, RHS can be written as:\n\n(x - 2021)(H_{2020} - H_{1999}) + 21\n\nSo now, equating LHS and RHS:\n\n(x - 2020) H_{21} + (21 - H_{21}) = (x - 2021)(H_{2020} - H_{1999}) + 21\n\nLet me write this equation out:\n\nLeft side: x H_{21} - 2020 H_{21} + 21 - H_{21}\n\nRight side: x (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) - 2021 (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) + 21\n\nSo bringing all terms to the left side:\n\nx H_{21} - 2020 H_{21} + 21 - H_{21} - x (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) + 2021 (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) - 21 = 0\n\nSimplify:\n\nx [ H_{21} - (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) ] + [ -2020 H_{21} + 21 - H_{21} + 2021 (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) - 21 ] = 0\n\nSimplify the constants:\n\n-2020 H_{21} - H_{21} + 21 -21 + 2021 (H_{2020} - H_{1999})\n\n= -2021 H_{21} + 2021 (H_{2020} - H_{1999})\n\nFactor out 2021:\n\n2021 [ (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) - H_{21} ]\n\nTherefore, the equation becomes:\n\nx [ H_{21} - (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) ] + 2021 [ (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) - H_{21} ] = 0\n\nFactor out [ (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) - H_{21} ]:\n\n[ (H_{2020} - H_{1999}) - H_{21} ] ( -x + 2021 ) = 0\n\nWait, let me see:\n\nThe equation is:\n\nx [ A - B ] + 2021 [ B - A ] = 0, where A = H_{21}, B = H_{2020} - H_{1999}\n\nSo that's x (A - B) - 2021 (A - B) = 0\n\nFactor out (A - B):\n\n(A - B)(x - 2021) = 0\n\nTherefore, either A - B = 0 or x - 2021 = 0.\n\nSo either:\n\n1. H_{21} = H_{2020} - H_{1999}, or\n\n2. x = 2021\n\nBut we need to check if H_{21} = H_{2020} - H_{1999} is true.\n\nWait, H_{2020} - H_{1999} is the sum from 2000 to 2020 of 1/k, which is sum_{k=2000}^{2020} 1/k. H_{21} is sum_{k=1}^{21} 1/k. These are two different harmonic series segments. Are they equal?\n\nAlmost certainly not. The harmonic series grows logarithmically, and the sum from 2000 to 2020 would be approximately ln(2020) - ln(1999) \u224