u2089\u2087\u2084 must be 0 (since |x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2084| = |x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2083 +1| = |-1 +1| =0. So x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2084 is 0.\n\nThen x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085 = \u00b11 (since |0 +1| =1). So we can choose x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085 =1 or -1. If we choose x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085 =1, then the sum of the last three terms is -1 +0 +1 =0. Therefore, total sum is -986 +0 = -986. So |Sum| =986. That's better than 988. So why did I think before that in Case B, sum was -2? Because I assumed choosing x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085=-1, but actually we can choose x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085=1. Therefore, this seems like a better choice. So in this case, the sum over the last three terms can be 0, leading to a total sum of -986, absolute value 986.\n\nBut wait, is this allowed? Let's confirm step by step.\n\nx\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2082 =0 (from the previous cycle end).\n\nx\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2083: |x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2083| = |0 +1| =1. So x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2083=\u00b11. Let's choose x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2083=-1.\n\nThen x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2084: |x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2084| = |-1 +1| =0. So x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2084=0.\n\nThen x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085: |x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085| = |0 +1| =1. So x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085=\u00b11. Choosing x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085=1.\n\nTherefore, sum of x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2083 +x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2084 +x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085 = -1 +0 +1=0. Therefore, total sum is -986 +0= -986. Hence, |Sum|=986.\n\nAlternatively, if we choose x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085=-1, sum is -1 +0 -1=-2, leading to |Sum|=988.\n\nTherefore, choosing x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2085=1 is better. So, perhaps the minimal sum in this case is 986.\n\nBut wait, is there a way to get even a lower sum? Let's think.\n\nSuppose in the last three terms, instead of following the cycle, we can choose different signs to get a smaller sum. But in this case, after x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2082=0, x\u2081\u2089\u2087\u2083 can be -1 or 1. Let's see both possibilities.\n\nCase A